# AoTv4 custom overlay: .devcontainer/custom/ holds the project's own source (custom Lua
# modules, global_player.lua edits, eq-core-dll source) which the Makefile applies onto the
# bootstrapped clones. Track it -- including the dll .vcxproj that the global *.vcxproj rule
# above would otherwise hide.
!.devcontainer/custom/**/*.vcxproj

# Large DB recovery dumps -- local backups only, never committed (see POST_REBUILD_RECOVERY.md)
/Deez.sql
/aotv4_current.sql
# Auto-generated migration pre-backup dumps (mysqldump, see CLAUDE.md §15) -- dated, 100s of MB, never commit
/peq_aotv4_*.sql
/peq_*_backup*.sql
client_dist/BaseData.txt
client_dist/dbstr_us.txt
client_dist/SkillCaps.txt
client_dist/spells_us.txt
aotv4_custom_spells.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- client UI XML (EQUI_*.xml)
# Stock and reference client UI files, wherever they land: the copies dropped at the repo root as
# SIDL references (EQUI_Animations, EQUI_Templates, EQUI_BazaarWnd, ...), a whole "default" uifiles
# folder copied in from the client, and anything under utils/. None of it is ours; every file is
# recoverable from any RoF2 install, and together they are thousands of lines of churn.
EQUI_*.xml
/default/
utils/EQUI_*.xml

# ⚠️ OUR OWN WINDOWS ARE NOT IGNORED, and must not be. The files below are hand-authored SOURCE and
# the repo is their only copy -- the dll looks each one up by screen name at runtime, so losing one
# means that window silently never appears again with no error anywhere. The blanket rule above
# would otherwise swallow them, because a pattern with no slash matches at ANY depth.
!aotv4_client_install/uifiles_default/EQUI_*.xml

# ...except the picker, which is GENERATED by aotv4_client_install/gen_choice_xml.pl from
# spell_icons.lua + skill_pool.lua. ~8600 lines that change wholesale on every pool regen; rerun the
# generator rather than diffing it.
aotv4_client_install/uifiles_default/EQUI_AoTSpellChoiceWnd.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local-only working files
# ⚠️⚠️ NOTHING BELOW THIS LINE MAY BE HAND-AUTHORED SOURCE. Everything here is a database dump, a
# large third-party import, or a generated artifact its own script can reproduce. This block used to
# be an unstructured pile of bare filenames appended one at a time, and it had rotted three ways:
#   - it listed `.gitignore` and `CLAUDE.md` (twice), i.e. ITSELF and the project's primary document.
#     Both survived only because git cannot untrack an already-tracked file, so the entries sat there
#     inert -- and would have silently dropped either file the moment it was removed and re-added.
#   - it listed `SPELL_RANKS.md`, which was NOT already tracked. That is the ONLY documentation of a
#     live system (spell ranks 1-5, Parchment Fragments, Ink of the Lost, keeping 2 spells through
#     death) -- CLAUDE.md does not mention any of it -- and it was one `rm` from being unrecoverable.
#   - it carried duplicates (`peq_pre_region_merge.sql.gz` twice).
# 📌 Add a PATTERN with a comment saying what produces the file, never a bare filename. A bare name
# with no slash matches at ANY depth, which is the same trap the EQUI_*.xml block above documents.

# Database dumps: pre-migration backups and recovery snapshots (CLAUDE.md §25). Tens of MB each.
# ⚠️ A small one is not a failed dump -- several are deliberately TABLE-SCOPED (peq_pre_all_race_class
# is one table, peq_pre_regions_011 is four). Verify with `gzip -dc x.gz | grep -c '^CREATE TABLE'`
# and the `Dump completed on` tail marker before trusting OR deleting any of them.
/peq_*.sql.gz

# Third-party SQL imports, applied once and then dead weight (aot_regions_0.1.1.sql is 32 MB).
/aot_regions_*.sql

# Generated analysis output -- rerun the tool rather than committing the CSV.
#   custom/spell_usage.csv  <- .devcontainer/custom/tools/spell_usage.pl
#   quest_turnins.csv       <- .devcontainer/custom/tools/quest_difficulty.pl
#   race_scaling.csv        <- the race scaling pass (§ base_data / aotv4_dungeon_scale)
/quest_turnins.csv
/race_scaling.csv
custom/spell_usage.csv

# Stock EQ client model archives (global_chr.s3d, global4_chr.s3d, ...). Same rule as the stock
# EQUI_*.xml above: not ours, and byte-recoverable from any RoF2 install.
# ⚠️ ROOT-SCOPED ON PURPOSE (`/*.s3d`, not `*.s3d`) so it cannot swallow an archive we deliberately
# ship under aotv4_client_install/.
# ⚠️⚠️ IF A MODEL ARCHIVE IS EVER MODIFIED FOR AoTv4, STILL DO NOT COMMIT THE REPACKED .s3d -- a
# multi-megabyte binary has no diff, no history and no way to rebuild it. Track the extracted
# textures plus a repack script and let the build produce the archive, exactly as
# aotv4_client_install/gen_choice_xml.pl generates the picker XML from spell_icons.lua.
/*.s3d
